  "text": "I can understand why you would feel angry. It's like, you're being told who you can and can't be friends with, and that can be really frustrating.\n\nWhen I was in a similar situation, I remember feeling really upset and angry too. But then I realized that my mom was coming from a place of love and concern, even if her methods weren't the best.\n\nI started talking to her about how I felt, and I explained to her that I understood where she was coming from, but I also needed some space to make my own choices. It wasn't easy, but we eventually found a way to compromise.\n\nOne thing that helped was when I asked her if she had ever made any mistakes when she was my age. She said yes, and that made me feel a little better. It made me realize that she wasn't perfect, and that she was trying her best.\n\nI also started to think about what I wanted to say to her, rather than just reacting with anger. I wanted to tell her that I loved her, but that I also needed some freedom to make my own choices.\n\nIt's not always easy, but talking to her and explaining how I felt really helped. And it's okay to feel angry, by the way. It's a normal feeling when you're in a situation like this.\n\nHow about you? Have you talked to your mom about how you feel?",
